From 5b720bb668e7551105feb9ad7b17c1de918f2c14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Yu <josephyu@yahooinc.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:09:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Let a phone app connect over WiFi on MUI devices

The socket API (TCP 4403) was skipped whenever displaymode is COLOR, so on MUI
boards a phone app could only ever connect over BLE - and device-ui's programming
mode turns WiFi off outright as part of that hand-off. mDNS still advertised 4403
regardless, so the node looked reachable and refused every connection.

The reason for the gate is real but narrower than the gate itself: the on-device
UI is a PhoneAPI client too (PacketAPI, polling every 10-50ms), and
MeshService::toPhoneQueue has a single destructive dequeue with no per-client
fan-out, so two clients steal packets from each other. Everything else in
PhoneAPI is already per-instance - state machine, fromRadioScratch, auth slot -
so only the live-packet drain actually needs arbitrating.

So arbitrate there instead of disabling the server: PhoneAPI::wantsLivePackets()
gates the toPhoneQueue drain, and PacketAPI overrides it to stand down while a
socket-API client is attached. The phone then receives every packet rather than
the two splitting them, and the UI reclaims the queue on its own when the phone
disconnects. Config download, request/response and heartbeats keep flowing to the
UI throughout, so the screen stays healthy - it just stops seeing new mesh
traffic while the phone is connected.

The client count lives in an inline function's local static rather than a global
in ServerAPI.cpp, because InterfacesTemplates.cpp #includes that .cpp to
instantiate the templates - a plain definition there is a duplicate symbol.

The web server stays gated: it needs an HTTPS/mbedTLS heap budget the LVGL
targets do not have, which is a separate problem from the queue.

Verified on a Heltec V4 TFT (heltec-v4-tft, 2.8.0.3c83c8d): flash unchanged at
97.6%, device boots clean, and a phone app connects over WiFi TCP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjqMrWWLWXvmh69rvGCEo
